# Chat 02: unsure -> it asks; the answer teaches it. ProbePala, party of two, filmed from {me}.
# Before each take: tools/cua/takes/forget-demo-phrases.sh (the learned phrase must not exist yet).
warp 104040000 140
darksight {me}
party {me} 0
offline ProbePala
say !spawnbot ProbePala
online ProbePala
party {me} 2
wait 8
park
record FriendServer/BotStory Server/docs/agents/evidence/video/2026-09-26/raw/chat-02-asks-then-learns.mp4
wait 1
cut
caption 6 When it isn't sure what the player means, it asks - and the answer teaches it
wait 2
say see all those snails? go clear em out
expectlog ACT \[grind\]
park
follow ProbePala 8
say ok that's plenty, ease off
expectlog ASK \[stop\]
park
caption 5 "ease off" is ambiguous, so it asks instead of guessing
wait 3
say yea
expectlog learned .* -> stop \(PLAYER
park
caption 5 "yea" - it stops and remembers what that phrase meant
wait 4
say alright, head back over to me
expectlog ASK \[follow me\]
park
caption 4 Unsure again - it asks
wait 3
say nah
park
caption 4 "nah" - it drops the suggestion
wait 3
say see all those snails? go clear em out
expectlog ACT \[grind\].*\n(.*\n)*.*ACT \[grind\]
park
follow ProbePala 8
say ok that's plenty, ease off
expectlog \[phrase\] message="ok that's plenty, ease off" -> stop
park
caption 6 Same phrase again - no question this time: it learned what the player meant
wait 5
stop
# Teardown (not recorded): sign off, dissolve the two-person party.
signoff ProbePala
say !leaveparty
party {me} 0
